    "public_api_change": "ADDITIVE",
    "schema_diff_summary": "edit.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Add is_delete on impl Edit. Keep it public, the same way is_insert is public. Do not add a dead_code attribute. The body is one condition: !self.old.is_empty() && self.new.is_empty(). Do not nest an if inside an if. Do not write two if arms that return the same value. Combine them with ||. That is clippy::if_same_then_else. Do not touch is_insert, insert, delete, old_end, new_end, delta, or invert. The existing test an_insert_has_no_old_text stays green. Do not rewrite its assertions. The test a_delete_has_no_new_text checks Edit::delete of ab is true. Edit::insert of ab is false. An edit with old a and new b is false. An edit with both strings empty is false. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Stay inside this one behavior. Do not add a second case for coherence. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
